  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Michael King shut down Atlanta over seven scoreless innings, and Manny Machado hit a solo homer to win it.",
    "what_this_means": "This was pitching duel baseball at its purest. One run through nine innings, King dominating the zone while the Padres scraped together four hits and a chance. That's the game. Nine strikeouts between the two teams, and Atlanta never threatened. What matters is that King gave the offense permission to win ugly. Machado delivered on that contract. The bullpen. Morejon and Mason Miller combining for two scoreless innings with four strikeouts. Never had to sweat. This is what efficient looks like when the starter erases doubt. One-run leads are fragile until they aren't. Today it held because no one had to ask the bullpen to do anything impossible.",
